# Cello Suite No. 3 in C major, BWV 1009: Prelude (J. S. Bach)
#
# Character: a grand, open-hearted C major prelude. It begins with a
# falling scale over two octaves to the low C, then streams in
# sixteenths: scales, arpeggios, and sequences through many keys, a long
# section over a held G pedal, rising scales to a climax, and a
# cadenza of separate chords with rests before the final return of the
# opening scale.
#
# Time signature: 3/4, 88 bars, no upbeat, no repeats. Mutopia file
# cellosuite3.mid, the first score of the set: checked against
# cellosuite3_1_prelude.ly (88 bars, last bar a quarter-note chord).
#
# Range: this score is at true pitch; 149 notes fall below B2 and are
# lifted an octave by the converter. It matters most in the G pedal
# section (45-60): the low G (G2) sounds as G3, so in bars 51-60 it
# lands on or above the notes it should sit under (G3, F3, E3). The
# pedal still repeats on every beat, but listen there: the effect is a
# repeated inner note rather than a deep pedal. The low C of bar 2 and
# the cadenza chords also lose their bottom octave, and four-note
# chords (77, 79, 80, 81-85, 88) keep three notes.
#
# Tempo: quarter = 80, 264 beats, about 3:20 with the cadenza and the
# final broadening. Track times: Mstislav Rostropovich (EMI, 1991)
# 3:23 to 3:24, about 78 overall; his 1955 Prague radio recording 3:57,
# about 67. Confirmed from track listings. Since the cadenza chords and
# the end are taken slower, the running sixteenths in such readings go
# a little faster than the average; 80 keeps them at 11 frames each.
#
# Structure (score bars, my reading of the Mutopia score):
#   1-6    The falling C major scale to the low C, then rising scales.
#   7-14   Sequence of scale figures through G and D; G major (13-14).
#   15-20  To A minor; E major dominant (20).
#   21-26  A minor, D sharp and G sharp figures; cadence (26-27).
#   27-36  Arpeggio sequence: A minor, G7, C7 (31), toward F, G7.
#   37-44  Falling arpeggio sequence over low roots: A minor, D minor,
#          B, E minor, C, F, D minor.
#   45-60  The G pedal: the dominant held under changing harmonies,
#          growing more dissonant (E flat, F sharp, 58-60).
#   61-70  Chromatic descent through C sharp, B, F sharp, B flat.
#   71-76  Rising scales to the high register, then the fall (76).
#   77-80  The cadenza: G7 chord, a falling run, diminished chord, G7,
#          each chord followed by rests.
#   81-86  Chords over a C pedal: C, C7, F, A flat, to G7 with a trill.
#   87-88  The opening scale returns; final C major chord.

tempo 80

dyn 1 f              # bars 1-14: the open, festive opening
dyn 15 mp            # bars 15-26: A minor, a softer colour
dyn 27 mf            # bars 27-44: the arpeggio sequences
dyn 45 p             # bars 45-60: the G pedal starts quietly and
ramp 45-60 f         # builds as the harmony tightens over it
dyn 61 mf            # bars 61-70: the chromatic descent
ramp 71-76 ff        # bars 71-76: the rising scales to the climax
dyn 77 ff            # bars 77-80: the cadenza chords
broaden 77-80 0.85   # each chord given room, as players do
dyn 81 f             # bars 81-86: chords over the C pedal
broaden 85-86 0.85   # the G7 and its trill before the return
dyn 87 ff            # bars 87-88: the opening scale and the last chord

rit 1 0.7            # the final scale slows into the chord
